[36m(TaskRunner pid=524197)[0m To find the value of \( m + n \) where \( \frac{m}{n} \) is the irreducible fraction of the expression:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=524197)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=524197)[0m \[ 3 + \frac{1}{3 + \frac{1}{3 + \frac{1}{3}}} \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=524197)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=524197)[0m we start by simplifying the innermost fraction and work our way outwards.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=524197)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=524197)[0m 1. Compute the innermost fraction:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=524197)[0m    \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=524197)[0m    3 + \frac{1}{3} = \frac{9}{3} + \frac{1}{3} = \frac{10}{3}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=524197)[0m    \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=524197)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=524197)[0m 2. Substitute this result into the next layer:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=524197)[0m    \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=524197)[0m    3 + \frac{1}{\frac{10}{3}} = 3 + \frac{3}{10} = \frac{30}{10} + \frac{3}{10} = \frac{33}{10}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=524197)[0m    \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=524197)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=524197)[0m 3. Substitute this result into the outermost layer:
[36m(TaskRunner pid=524197)[0m    \[
[36m(TaskRunner pid=524197)[0m    3 + \frac{1}{\frac{33}{10}} = 3 + \frac{10}{33} = \frac{99}{33} + \frac{10}{33} = \frac{109}{33}
[36m(TaskRunner pid=524197)[0m    \]
[36m(TaskRunner pid=524197)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=524197)[0m The fraction \( \frac{109}{33} \) is irreducible since 109 is a prime number and does not share any common factors with 33 other than 1.
[36m(TaskRunner pid=524197)[0m 
[36m(TaskRunner pid=524197)[0m Thus, \( m = 109 \) and \( n = 33 \), so \( m + n = 109 + 33 = 142 \).
