[36m(TaskRunner pid=524197)[0m Aya walks 9 kilometers every morning. When she walks at a constant speed of \( s \) kilometers per hour, the walk takes her 4 hours, including \( t \) minutes spent in the coffee shop. When she walks at \( s + 2 \) kilometers per hour, the walk takes her 2 hours and 24 minutes, including \( t \) minutes. We need to find the number of minutes the walk takes her, including \( t \) minutes, when she walks at \( s + \frac{1}{2} \) kilometers per hour.
